    "result_text": "All 257 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS. The failure-looking stack trace line is just a logged exception from an existing negative test (`createUserNoRolesFails`), which reports 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional, region-validated `postcode` field to owners, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema: `type: string`, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`, not in `required`. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with the field, and bean validation rejects a malformed (non-4-digit) postcode with **400** automatically. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, it's both accepted on write and returned on read.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner.java`: added `postcode` field with `@Column`, getter/setter.\n- Added the `postcode` column to all DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) and fixed the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the test DB) to supply the extra value.\n\n**Region validation** (OfficeFloor function pipeline)\n- `PostcodeRegions.java`: the fixed tables \u2014 Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD; NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n- `RejectInvalidPostcode.java`: a step that skips when postcode is absent/blank, otherwise throws the checked `InvalidPostcodeException` when out of range for the city's region.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2192 responds **400**.\n- Wired `rejectInvalidPostcode` into `owners.POST.yml` (after address normalization) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`; added postcode copy to `ApplyOwner` so the update path stores/validates it too.\n\nThe mapper maps `postcode` by name automatically, so it's stored and returned when given.\n\nOne catch I hit and fixed: `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws `NPE` on a null key, so an unknown-region city initially caused a 500 \u2014 `isValid` now short-circuits on a null region.",
